### 4.1 — `src/components/AppLayout.tsx` — Sidebar Persistence

**Current state:** `SidebarProvider` (in `AppLayout.tsx`) uses `defaultOpen={true}` (the `sidebar.tsx` component default at line 50). The `SidebarProvider` already writes a cookie named `sidebar:state` when toggled (line 68 of sidebar.tsx). But `AppLayout.tsx` does not read that cookie to set `defaultOpen`.

**What to change:**
In `AppLayout.tsx`, read the cookie before rendering:

```typescript
function getSidebarDefaultOpen(): boolean {
  const match = document.cookie
    .split(";")
    .find((c) => c.trim().startsWith("sidebar:state="));
  if (!match) return true; // default open
  return match.split("=")[1]?.trim() === "true";
}

export function AppLayout() {
  const defaultOpen = getSidebarDefaultOpen();
  return (
    <SidebarProvider defaultOpen={defaultOpen}>
      {/* rest unchanged */}
    </SidebarProvider>
  );
}
```

This is safe because the cookie is already being written by the existing sidebar code. No external dependency needed.

